  "question": {
    "text": "At the sea level, the dry air mass percentage composition is given as nitrogen gas : 70.0, oxygen gas : 27.0 and argon gas : 3.0. If total pressure is 1.15 atm , then calculate the ratio of followings respectively :<br />(i) partial pressure of nitrogen gas to partial pressure of oxygen gas<br />(ii) partial pressure of oxygen gas to partial pressure of argon gas<br />(Given : Molar mass of $\\mathrm{N}, \\mathrm{O}$ and Ar are 14, 16, and $40 \\mathrm{~g} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$ respectively)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "72LKZ",
      "text": "$4.26,19.3$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SVkTF",
      "text": "$2.59,11.85$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "vwzjA",
      "text": "$5.46,17.8$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "u0kKQ",
      "text": "$2.96,11.2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\frac{\\mathrm{P}_{\\mathrm{N}_2}}{\\mathrm{Po}_2}=\\frac{\\mathrm{x}_{\\mathrm{N}_2} \\cdot \\mathrm{P}_{\\mathrm{T}}}{\\mathrm{x}_{\\mathrm{O}_2} \\cdot \\mathrm{P}_{\\mathrm{T}}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{n}_{\\mathrm{N}_2}}{\\mathrm{n}_{\\mathrm{O}_2}}$ {using Dalton's law of partial pressure}<br />$\\begin{aligned} & =\\frac{70 / 28}{27 / 32}=2.96 \\\\ & \\frac{\\mathrm{P}_{\\mathrm{O}_2}}{\\mathrm{P}_{\\mathrm{Ar}}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{n}_{\\mathrm{O}_2}}{\\mathrm{n}_{\\mathrm{Ar}}}=\\frac{27 / 32}{3 / 40}=11.25\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
